chunk_findings.detail:
The adjacency test is tightened to `argv[first] == stray[0]`, but the suggestion still joins *every* unrecognized word: `','.join([value, *stray])`. argparse reports all extras in source order, so for
`ddflow update T1 --globs a.py b.py --tags x y`
the message is `unrecognized arguments: b.py y`, `stray == ["b.py", "y"]`, the adjacency check passes on `b.py`, and the hint emitted is `--globs takes ONE value, a comma-separated list (--globs a.py,b.py,y)`. That folds `y` — an unrecognized word that followed `--tags`, which the new docstring promises will "get the plain error" — into the globs list, and following the advice would drop `y` from `--tags`. Only the strays contiguous with the glob value should be joined into the suggestion (at minimum, strays belonging to another flag should not be);

